    "final_summary": "web1 (10.10.40.10) was the only failing endpoint — all pairs touching it failed both directions while app1 (10.10.50.10) worked. Root cause on fw-ext: the DMZ firewall zone listed only interface eth3 (dmz_app); eth2 (10.10.40.1/24, the web1 gateway) was a member of no zone, so web1's traffic was dropped even though the INTERNAL-TO-DMZ / DMZ-TO-INTERNAL / OUTSIDE-TO-DMZ / DMZ-TO-OUTSIDE rulesets already contained the intended allow rules for web1. Applied one narrow fix: set firewall zone DMZ interface eth2 (transaction ani_tx_f2984ec9f69c9e45), putting the interface back in its zone without loosening any default action, rule, or other interface. Re-validation of public_success_criteria passed: all 10 connectivity pairs succeed, including user1<->web1, guest1<->web1, external1<->web1, with the healthy app1 paths unchanged.",
